rivedin (EI 4), same as Tripāṭhin; epithet of Brāhmaṇas later stereotyped as family name.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "triviDaksitisacuqamaRi": [{"id": "triviDakzitISacUqAmaRi", "headword": "त्रिविधक्षितीशचूडामणि", "headword_slp1": "triviDakzitISacUqAmaRi", "fold": "triviDaksitisacuqamaRi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "Trividha-kṣitīśa-cūḍāmaṇi (IE 8-2), epithet of a king probably [] referring to the Aśvapati, Gajapati and Narapati types of rulers, i. e. those who were strong in elephants, cavalry and infantry respectively.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "trisulakasu": [{"id": "triSUlakASu", "headword": "त्रिशूलकाशु", "headword_slp1": "triSUlakASu", "fold": "trisulakasu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "triśūla-kāśu , probably, ‘kāśu bearing the representation of a trident’; possibly issued by the authorities of a Śiva temple; see kāśu.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}]}